          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            We discuss in detail the realization of the abstract concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiber+sequences"} cofiber sequences
            in its explicit incarnation in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            textbooks.
          %p
            Hence we use the concepts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            instead of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            see instead at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Theory
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Homotopy+Theory#HomotopyFiberSequences"} Homotopy fiber sequences
          %h2#background Background
          %p
            Throughout, write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \coloneqq [0,1] \subset \mathbb{R}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
            equipped with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
          %h3#homotopy_equivalences Homotopy equivalences
          #LeftHomotopy.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
