          #MappingConePasting.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In summary, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConeCyclinder"}
              and def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MappingConeCylinder"}
              say that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              then we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              diagrams in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              of the following form:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi po
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi Cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Cyl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi po
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi po
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Cone
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Cone
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_1}} &amp;(po)&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{i_0}{\to}&amp; Cyl(X) &amp;\to &amp; Cyl(f)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;(po)&amp; \downarrow &amp;(po)&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    {*} &amp;\to&amp; Cone(X) &amp;\to&amp; Cone(f)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Cone(X)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+Hurewicz+cofibration"} closed Hurewicz cofibration
              , the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              together with prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantHomotopyEquivalencePushout"}
              therefore implies that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
